    {
      "id": 477020,
      "username": "asjadkhan",
      "name": "Asjadkhan",
      "created_at": "2025-08-11T09:14:19.048Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This happens because ERPNext’s purchase receipt quality inspection logic checks the entire document’s items table, not just the “Quality Inspection Required” flag for a single row, so the system ends up generating inspections for all items in the receipt.</p>\n<p>If you want inspections only for specific items, you’ll need to either:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Manually remove</strong> the extra inspection rows before submission, or</li>\n<li><strong>Customize the workflow/script</strong> to filter <code>items</code> by <code>quality_inspection_required</code> before creating inspections.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This is a known behavior—ERPNext doesn’t currently auto-skip non-flagged items unless custom logic is added.</p>",
